  {
    "question": "What does the Gold Standard define as “good standing” for an entity providing documentation in the Project Documentation?",
    "answer": "Good standing is defined as being a legal or other appropriate entity registered in or allowed to operate within the required jurisdiction and with no evidence of insolvency or legal/criminal notices placed against it or any of its Directors."
  },
  {
    "question": "Under the Gold Standard, what must be demonstrated for full and uncontested legal ownership of products such as carbon credits, and what additional consent is required when ownership is transferred?",
    "answer": "Full and uncontested legal ownership shall be demonstrated, and when ownership is transferred from project beneficiaries it must be demonstrated transparently and with full, prior and informed consent (FPIC)."
  }
]

